//! Type checking for full Kio (System F core + the elaboration-aware
//! positions `if`/`else`, user-elaborator calls, and field syntax).
//!
//! Most of the typer machinery is shared with the kio-prime binary's
//! standalone Kio'-only typer through [`crate::pass::typecheck_core`]
//! (`ModuleEnv<P>`, `TypeCtx<P>`, the synth/check/apply family,
//! the `Typer<P>` dispatch trait, …). This module retains only the
//! pieces that depend on the elaboration table — conditional elaboration construction,
//! user-elaborator action preparation, `synth_field_access` / `synth_field_update`
//! — plus the [`Elaborations`]
//! type itself and the `LoweredTyper` that wires `Typer<Lowered>`
//! to the elaboration-aware `synth_expr` / `check_value_against`.
//! The `kio` binary's [`check_package`] entry point at the bottom drives the
//! shared scoped package checker, retains the normalized tree and elaborations
//! as one [`CheckedLoweredPackage`], substitutes through that proof-bearing
//! exit, then validates the resulting Prime package with the standalone Kio'
//! typer.
//!
//! This module runs after name resolution. It checks every top-level `fn` body
//! directly against its declared return type, while subexpressions synthesize
//! or check according to their local bidirectional position.
//!
//! Scope:
//!
//! - Core types: `()` / `!` / function arrow / product `(A & B)` /
//!   sum `(A | B)` / type-parameter references / alias
//!   references (intra-module + cross-module via `import`).
//! - Fns: `fn` / `fn` with mixed type-and-value parameters,
//!   `let`, `Call` with positional type and value arguments,
//!   polymorphic instantiation at call sites.
//! - Intrinsics: the eight value intrinsics (`__left__`,
//!   `__right__`, `__either__`, `__pair__`, `__fst__`,
//!   `__snd__`, `__if_then_else__`, `__absurd__`) typed against
//!   their schemes when `import __intrinsics__;` is in scope.
//! - Newtypes: constructor and projector member access (a newtype
//!   declaration is itself the iso-recursive boundary, so the
//!   payload is taken as-written when materializing the constructor
//!   input / projector output type); strict-positivity check on
//!   self-references in newtype payloads (rejecting any occurrence
//!   under the left of a `->`, including those revealed by intra-
//!   module alias unfolding).
//! - Literals: `StrLit` / `IntLit` / `FloatLit` / `BoolLit` typed
//!   against a `role(...)` host type by three-tier resolution
//!   (`synth_literal` / `resolve_literal_against`).
//! - Cross-module imports: `import m(foo);` / `import m(Foo);`
//!   are validated and their schemes flow through to the
//!   consuming module; host items are ambient for their
//!   owning root tree.
//! - Elaborator-position elaborations (`if`/`else`, internal
//!   elaboration forms, and user-defined elaborator calls) recorded
//!   in [`Elaborations`] and substituted into the AST during the
//!   `Lowered → Prime` transition by `crate::pass::substitute`.
//! - Export signatures validated against the package
//!   file's host.
//!
//! Type equality is structural up to visible alias unfolding, including aliases
//! imported from other modules. A
//! complete polymorphic function scheme is an ordinary structural value type
//! and may occupy any slot whose declared type is that complete scheme. A
//! genuinely monomorphic slot still rejects a polymorphic value.
//!
//! Call-argument parsing is intentionally permissive; type-argument
//! slots reinterpret value-shaped syntax through shared typecheck_core
//! helpers so functions, dot-splice calls, elaborator forms, and user
//! elaborators agree on the same boundary behavior.

